      "message": "This makes get_batt_conf block up to 2 secs. How would that affect the existing callers? Also, while sleeping at line 248, another thread may call get_batt_conf. Are we handling cuncurrency properly?\n\nHow about returning NULL immediately if init_battery_type fails? The existing callers need to handle NULL. For example, board_cut_off_battery already does so.\n\nI thought we want something like this:\n\n    static bool need_retry \u003d true.\n\n    const struct batt_conf_embed *get_batt_conf(void)\n    {\n        if (need_retry \u0026\u0026 !timestamp_expired())\n            need_retry \u003d init_battery_type;\n        return battery_conf;\n    }\n    \nThe suggested change needs a large view. Please let me know if it\u0027s beyond your current scope.",
